# The guest's whole allowlist. Anything not named here is refused at the proxy,
# and the guest firewall drops everything that is not the proxy port, so this file
# is the only place egress is widened.
#
# A line starting with a dot matches that domain and every subdomain; a bare name
# matches exactly. Add a host only with the reason it is needed.

# The Nix toolchain: the installer script, then the binary cache and its CDN.
.determinate.systems
.nixos.org

# Flake inputs and clones (pi, home-manager, firstmate, the work).
github.com
.codeload.github.com
.raw.githubusercontent.com

# The crew's own tools and harness downloads. pi fetches its own bundle at build
# time, so its vendor host is a build dependency, not a convenience.
.herdr.dev
.pi.dev

# GitHub serves release assets from a separate CDN host: the crew tools are
# release binaries, so this is a build dependency, not a convenience.
.release-assets.githubusercontent.com
.objects.githubusercontent.com

# npm tarballs for the pinned CLIs.
.registry.npmjs.org
